---
.title = "Hash Map (HashMap)",
.date = "2026-10-01",
.author = "ZigCC",
.layout = "section.shtml",
---

`std.AutoHashMap` is the standard key-value map in Zig, automatically deriving hashing and equality strategies for the key type. For string slice keys, `std.StringHashMap` is also available.

Common operations:
- `init(allocator)`: Initialize the hash map;
- `put(key, value)`: Insert or update a key-value entry;
- `get(key)`: Retrieve value by key (returns `null` if not found);
- `contains(key)`: Check whether a key is present;
- `getOrPut(key)`: Find an existing entry or allocate a new entry in-place;
- `remove(key)`: Remove entry by key;
- `iterator()`: Create an iterator over all key-value entries;
- `deinit()`: Free all allocated hash table memory.

